--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI QuickStatsPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state
holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable QuickStatsPageDataSource
seam whose value types mirror the three web hooks 1:1 (production binds the KMP repos /
use-cases: GET /vehicles, GET /analytics/fleet?days=30, GET /vehicles/{id}/state through
the seam). There are no charts and no map (manifest declares 0/0).

The page is a compact "kiosk" surface reproducing the web chrome (PageContainer title +
its loading / error phases) and BOTH web regions:

  GlassPanel1 — the vehicle header card: a tinted car glyph + the vehicle name
    (web `display_name || 'Tesla'`) + the "model · connection" subtitle, OR — when no
    vehicle resolves — the localized no-vehicle EmptyState (ContentUnavailableView). Never
    hidden; always one or the other so the region is never blank.
  The 4 MetricCards — Distance ("{{unit}} Driven") / Drives / Energy ("kWh Used") /
    Cost ("Total Cost"), each a TSCard with a muted label over a large primary value,
    matching the web `MetricCard` used WITHOUT an icon. They ALWAYS render with the web
    `?? 0` fallbacks (never gated behind data).

NAMING NOTE (no predecessor bypass): a PRE-EXISTING dashboard-widget feature-view,
TeslaSync/feature-views/QuickStatsGrid.*, already owns an entire `QuickStats*` type
namespace in the same app module (incl. `QuickStatsVehicleState` and `QuickStatsFormat`).
To avoid editing that sibling, EVERY new page type is prefixed `QuickStatsPage*`
(QuickStatsPageVehicle / …VehicleState / …Summary / …Phase / …DataSource / …Format /
…MetricCard / …MetricGrid / …VehicleCard / …Footer / …Skeleton, + Sample/Empty/NoVehicle/
Failing…PageDataSource). Verified collision-free module-wide before + after the full build.

Units (ADR-005): the distance card reads SI metres and converts to the user's unit ONLY at
the render boundary via the shared `Units` facade (KMP) + QuickStatsPageFormat; energy is
pinned to kWh and cost to currency exactly as the web hardcodes those labels. Nothing
non-SI is stored or computed.

Adaptive across macOS/iPad (regular) + iPhone (compact): a centred, width-capped (440pt)
ScrollView column; the metric grid reflows 1↔2 columns via the `#if os(iOS)`
horizontalSizeClass branch (web `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2`). VoiceOver labels/headers
(.isHeader on the name, combined metric cards, .isLink on the footer link), Dynamic Type
(token fonts), light/dark + increased-contrast via the P2 tokens.

Files (all new unless noted):
  Sources/Features/Dashboard/QuickStatsModels.swift            (vehicle/state/summary/phase/datasource)
  Sources/Features/Dashboard/QuickStatsFormat.swift           (display-boundary formatters)
  Sources/Features/Dashboard/QuickStatsPageModel.swift        (@Observable model — load/refresh/states)
  Sources/Features/Dashboard/QuickStatsPageModel.Sample.swift (sample + preview/test seams)
  Sources/Features/Dashboard/QuickStatsPage.swift             (view: phase switch + ready column + previews)
  Sources/Features/Dashboard/QuickStatsPage.Sections.swift    (vehicle card / metric card+grid / footer / skeleton)
  Sources/Features/Dashboard/QuickStatsRouteRegistration.swift (.quickStats route registration)
  Tests/Unit/Features/Dashboard/QuickStatsPageModelTests.swift (state-machine + formatter + route tests)
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift          (MOD: +.quickStats case / pathSegment "quick-stats" / icon / Overview group)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift          (MOD: wire QuickStatsRouteRegistration after the Glance registration)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings  (MOD: +10 keys = 9 web parity literals + route.quickStats)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json       (MOD: +2 rows page:dashboard/QuickStats 18/18, apple-macos + apple-ios)

Navigation: the web route /quick-stats maps 1:1 to AppRoute.quickStats (pathSegment
"quick-stats"), so AppRouteParser resolves it directly with NO alias needed. `.quickStats`
is added to the Overview sidebar group (web standalone route) and is reachable +
deep-linkable. The only exhaustive AppRoute switches live in AppRoute.swift (systemImage +
group); WatchDeepLink is its own enum and is unaffected. The web footer "Open Dashboard"
link is wired to the shell via onOpenDashboard -> selection = .dashboard.

i18n: every visible literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings using the WEB key names
verbatim (quickStats.*). The distance card's `{{unit}} Driven` i18next interpolation is
reproduced via String(localized: "quickStats.distance") + replacingOccurrences(of:
"{{unit}}", with: units.distance) — faithful to the web, like the sibling APIKeys {{name}}.
The connection token ("online"/"asleep"/…, default "offline") is rendered verbatim as a
DATA value (matching the web's bare `?? 'offline'`), so it is not a hardcoded UI literal.
Zero hardcoded user-facing strings.

